# LLM / Grok integration

- One thin client module wraps the provider SDK; everything else depends on an interface (bring-your-own-model stays possible).
- Model id, temperature, max tokens, and seed (where supported) come from config, are logged per run, and appear in every results table.
- Every call records tokens in/out, latency, cost estimate, and model id to the run ledger (agent-cost-attribution format).
- Timeouts and retries are explicit and bounded; on exhaustion the caller gets a fail-closed result, not a guess.
- Structured outputs are schema-validated; a validation failure is a refusal, not a best-effort parse.
- Tests use recorded fixtures or a fake client; no live calls in CI.
- API keys only from env (`XAI_API_KEY`); never committed, never echoed.
